{"name":"Ducal Pink","hex":"#ce9096","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"ducal","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of or pertaining to a duke, a duchess, or the duchy or dukedom they hold."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ducal"},{"term":"pink","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A color reminiscent of pinks, the flowers.","Magenta, the colour evoked by red and blue light when combined."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a colour between red and white; pale red.","Of a fox-hunter's jacket: scarlet."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pink"}],"entries":[{"title":"Duke","blocks":[{"text":"Duke is a male title either of a monarch ruling over a duchy, or of a member of royalty, or nobility. As rulers, dukes are ranked below emperors, kings, grand princes, grand dukes, and above sovereign princes. As royalty or nobility, they are ranked below grand dukes and above or below princes, depending on the country or specific title. The title comes from French duc, itself from the Latin dux, 'leader', a term used in republican Rome to refer to a military commander without an official rank, and later coming to mean the leading military commander of a province. In most countries, the word duchess is the female equivalent."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/James_Brydges%2C_1st_Duke_of_Chandos_by_Michael_Dahl.jpg/330px-James_Brydges%2C_1st_Duke_of_Chandos_by_Michael_Dahl.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Duke"},{"title":"Pink","blocks":[{"text":"Pink is a pale tint of red or rose, the color of the pink flower. It was first used as a color name in the late 17th century. A combination of pink and white is associated with innocence, whereas a combination of pink and black links to eroticism and seduction."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Pink_sapphire_